Add or update a Microsoft Foundry project.

Use --new-project --acr-resource-id to reuse an external registry for
source-built agents with Bicep. Project-only setup saves the selection
until agents are added. Code, prebuilt-image, and non-container-only
projects cannot use the selector. A deployed registry binding cannot
be changed; repeating the same selection preserves the project.
The registry must be in the project's subscription and outside its
resource group. Cross-subscription reuse is not supported.

Usage
  azd ai project add [flags]

Flags
      --acr-resource-id string  : External registry ARM resource ID for --new-project source builds (same subscription; Bicep only; no migration)
      --force                   : Replace a different configured project
      --infra string[="bicep"]  : Eject Bicep or Terraform infrastructure (optional value)
      --new-project             : Create a new Foundry project
      --project-endpoint string : Existing Foundry project endpoint
      --project-id string       : Existing Foundry project ARM resource ID

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for add
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (supported: default, json, none) (default "default")

Examples
  Configure a Foundry project interactively
    azd ai project add

  Connect an existing project by its ARM resource ID
    azd ai project add --project-id "<project-resource-id>"

  Reuse an externally owned registry for source-built agents (Bicep only)
    azd ai project add --new-project --acr-resource-id "<registry-resource-id>"

  Eject the configured infrastructure as Bicep
    azd ai project add --infra=bicep
